From: Debian MbedTLS 3.6.6 patch 100-fix-gcc14-build.patch (backported to 3.6.5)
Origin: https://sources.debian.org/patches/mbedtls/3.6.6-0.1~deb13u1/100-fix-gcc14-build.patch/
Bug: https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls/issues/9003
Rationale: GCC 14 incorrectly diagnoses the byte-at-a-time tail after an exact SIMD-sized block.

--- a/library/common.h
+++ b/library/common.h
@@ -190 +190 @@
-#if defined(__IAR_SYSTEMS_ICC__)
+#if defined(__IAR_SYSTEMS_ICC__) || (defined(MBEDTLS_COMPILER_IS_GCC) && MBEDTLS_GCC_VERSION >= 140100)
